	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "N2lFgE5MF3S2DI4Fn",
			"markdown": "**SURUBASH (herd-head), 44 - the best mirror in the party**\n\nLay Turchin (those-whose-work-is-the-aurochs). No grade, no licence, no doctrine. He is here to handle dogs.\n\n**He goes into Qara (black; the lead bitch) awake, deliberately, and comes back when he chooses.** No word for it, no theory, no anxiety - which makes him Stürm's exact opposite. One rung above the PC on that axis and one axis only: **Animal Companion [5] + Warg [15], and no Green Sight, no Warg Dreams, no day-knowing at all. Never give him Skinchanger.**\n\nCanon: `characters/sturm/canon/Yak.md` sec.7-8, `The_Yol.md`. Rules: `characters/sturm/mechanics/GURPS_GOT_Wargs_Skinchangers_GreenSight_.pdf`. Closes half of BACKLOG E4.",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "ngKJiN4CjnLwZrgH_",
					"markdown": "**Warging Qara on-screen, step by step.** 1 second of Concentration. His body drops where it is - unconscious, unaware, and somebody has to be told to sit with it. He then plays Qara: her ST/DX/HT, her Move, her nose, his IQ 10, his Will 12, his skills where they can apply. He comes back automatically, whenever he wants, no roll. The only thing that ends it against his will is a Major Wound or crippling injury to her - then he is back in his own body instantly and down 1 FP.\n\n**No Quick Contest.** That is Warg Dreams (Stürm's involuntary 1-in-6 nights). Surubash simply takes her, because she has been his for eleven years."
				},
				{
					"id": "naSBiYbYfcRjyjS_r",
					"markdown": "**Why the dogs are like that.** Nine dog-wolves that do not bark, do not fight, and cut angles - because someone is occasionally in one of them. Nobody in the column has worked this out, because the drovers are lay, unimportant, and walk out on the flanks where the priests are not looking. A Locke kennelmaster will call it witchcraft by day six.\n\n*\"You are asking me how. I do not know how. I know where the herd is. Go and ask the old woman your questions, she likes them.\"*"
				}
			]
		}
	],
